    multi-dump: tracks can belong to N dumps
    
    Allow a track to be assigned to multiple dumps instead of just one. This
    changes the DynamoDB layout to use TRACK_DUMP#<trackId>#<dumpId> sibling
    rows pointing at DUMP# GSI1 partitions, with per-dump ordering on the
    sibling row. The main TRACK# row now always lives on GSI1PK=TRACKS and
    carries a dumpIds: string[] field instead of a single dumpId.
    
    Reads are backwards compatible: itemToTrack normalizes legacy dumpId into
    dumpIds. Writes are backwards compatible on the way out: saveTrack diffs
    old vs new dumpIds and creates/removes sibling rows, and saveTracks (used
    by the GET merge pass) idempotently upserts sibling rows so legacy data
    migrates the first time the admin panel loads.
    
    Cascading publish state now ORs across every dump the track belongs to.
    Dump deletion cleans up all sibling rows and rewrites any legacy main rows
    that still live on its GSI1 partition.
    
    UI:
    - Tracks tab row: the single-dump dropdown is replaced by a compact
      multi-select disclosure with checkboxes.
    - Track edit modal: a "Dumps" section with a checkbox list of all dumps.
    - Dump edit modal: a new "Add existing tracks to this dump" section that
      mirrors the perm-checkbox lists, letting admins toggle tracks in and
      out of the dump.
    
    Public playlist: queue is deduped by track id so a multi-dump track only
    plays once and the index map stays consistent.
    
